KSHIFTLW/KSHIFTRW: shift is valid at count 15, not only below it

The SDM's pseudocode for the 16-bit opmask shifts is

    IF COUNT <= 15 THEN DEST[15:0] := SRC << COUNT ELSE DEST := 0

but Bochs guards them with `count < 15`, so `kshiftlw k1, k0, 15` — the
idiomatic "isolate the top mask bit" — yields 0 instead of 0x8000. A pure
typo: the 8/32/64-bit siblings in avx512_mask8/32/64.cc all use
`count < width`.

Found by this crate's differential suite; see docs/backend-differences.md
§4g. Still present on upstream master as of 2026-08-19 (d5c0ad9), unlike the
VPCONFLICT bug the same campaign found, which upstream fixed on 2026-06-09.

The hunks below are deliberately comment-free, so that this file can be sent
upstream as-is.

--- a/cpu/avx/avx512_mask16.cc
+++ b/cpu/avx/avx512_mask16.cc
@@ -157,7 +157,7 @@
 #if BX_SUPPORT_EVEX
   unsigned count = i->Ib();
   Bit16u opmask = 0;
-  if (count < 15)
+  if (count < 16)
     opmask = BX_READ_16BIT_OPMASK(i->src()) << count;
 
   BX_WRITE_OPMASK(i->dst(), opmask);
@@ -171,7 +171,7 @@
 #if BX_SUPPORT_EVEX
   unsigned count = i->Ib();
   Bit16u opmask = 0;
-  if (count < 15)
+  if (count < 16)
     opmask = BX_READ_16BIT_OPMASK(i->src()) >> count;
 
   BX_WRITE_OPMASK(i->dst(), opmask);
